## M0. Introduction — From the Pilot to the Deployment
*Function: establish the access problem, the pilot's withheld verdict, the institutional resolution,
and the section's claim — as a continuation of Parts I–II, not a standalone empirical paper.*
`MAP:` absorbs parts of §III.0.1/.5 and §III.3.1.

- **M0.1 The access problem and the pilot's restraint.** Clinical immersion is structurally scarce;
  the published VR case (appendix) established presence ≠ preference and deliberately withheld any
  pedagogical-effectiveness verdict — the study the pilot's limitations called for is this one.
  `[REUSE-COMPRESS: VR article — ~2 paragraphs max, cited to appendix]` `[ANCHOR: deployment-brief §1]`
- **M0.2 The institutional resolution as ontological fact.** State the record plainly first
  (AUTHOR-CONFIRMED 2026-07-15): the move to a 2D-PC-primary deployment was driven by VR scaling
  limitations — acquiring and distributing 120+ Meta Quest headsets to students every quarter was
  simply not possible; PC was chosen first as the largest student platform population (vs. Mac).
  THEN the reading: this pragmatic constraint is itself ontologically instructive — availability is
  an A₀-level condition (a world no student can enter discloses nothing), and the scaling wall is
  where the field's own literature locates it (→ M1.4, Radianti). Downstream fact to carry, not
  argue here: the deployment is fully online/asynchronous, so scheduled co-present time gives way
  to self-paced distributed time (chronos reconfigured — H2 demoted to framing; harvested at M3.5's
  activation-energy finding). `[ANCHOR: deployment-brief §2; author correction 2026-07-15]`
  `[PART I–II: A₀ ontological horizon; chronos (Part I §3.4)]`
- **M0.3 The claim.** State H1 + H3-clause + the WE thesis in one movement: the desktop world
  discloses (presence attested on screens) but does not complete (A₃→A₄ stall); its warrant against
  the video of itself is what video cannot render — place, task, and above all the WE, the one
  disclosive register the desktop alone possesses. `[NEW — the section's thesis statement]`
  `[PART I–II: rhetorical incorporation, dual being; veri(dis)similitude]`
- **M0.4 Jurisdiction and roadmap.** One paragraph on stance: a reanalysis through the frame
  (RODA bounded to episodes; the chain as background grammar; FE/P provenance discipline), then the
  section map. `[ANCHOR: cross-case-synthesis provenance rules]` `[PART I–II: RODA (Part II §2)]`

## M1. Background — The Desktop Route in the Literature
*Function: frame the desktop environment as a deliberate pedagogical modality with its own
affordance profile — never a degraded HMD. Establish continuity between the education literature's
own findings and the dissertation's frame.* **This module is the primary [LIT-SLOT] zone — every
sub-module is provisional until the incoming index entry is perused.**
`MAP:` new module (existing outline has no literature-review movement; §III.0.2–.3 gesture at Mark only).

- **M1.1 Desktop 3D as a modality in its own right.** Affordances derive from representational +
  interaction fidelity, not HMD hardware (Dalgarno & Lee); "pedagogical immersion" as a
  learning-design construct (Fowler); desktop-specific dual pathways — affective (presence→motivation)
  and cognitive (usability→) (Makransky & Petersen 2019; Merchant 2012). `[LIT-SLOT]`
- **M1.2 Presence on screens, and the missing bridge.** Medium-general presence (Lombard & Ditton —
  continuity with the VR article's own anchor); immersion-as-psychological-state (Witmer & Singer);
  Calleja's incorporation as the education literature's unmade bridge — which Part II has already
  built, and this section cashes empirically. `[LIT-SLOT]` `[PART I–II: presence-as-floor (Part II §3);
  incorporation re-grounded (Part II §2)]`
- **M1.3 More presence is not more learning.** The comparison evidence (Makransky/Terkildsen/Mayer;
  Parong & Mayer; Barrett's three-way equivalence) as the field's empirical mirror of
  presence≠incorporation; the skills-yield of screen-based virtual patients (Kononowicz; Cook) as
  evidence the modality's value lives in *doing*. `[LIT-SLOT]` `[PART I–II: presence as floor]`
- **M1.4 The asynchronous/scale/equity rationale.** Home ≡ classroom equivalence for desktop
  simulation (Petersen et al.); the HMD scalability gap as structural (Radianti); cybersickness
  (Cossio). Positions M0.2's institutional resolution inside the field's own trajectory. `[LIT-SLOT]`
- **M1.5 Boredom and engagement in educational VLEs.** Boredom in educational settings read
  Heideggerianly (Gibbs's ontological pedagogy; Mansikka; Feldges); the regulatory-signal corrective
  (Elpidorou) — episodic boredom is information, not verdict; the misattribution warning (Mertel;
  Thomson) — ask what the platform individualized before concluding students weren't trying.
  `[LIT-SLOT — expects growth from incoming entry]` `[ANCHOR: boredom-cluster mapping Roles 1–3]`
  `[PART I–II: boredom as orekton-to-be-fled (Part II §2); FCM second form (Part II §5)]`
- **M1.6 Learning together in shared virtual space.** (Adopted 2026-07-16.) Social presence as a
  construct in its own right, distinct from spatial presence (Biocca, Burgoon & Harms's criteria for
  a robust theory); its predictive weight for satisfaction and perceived learning (Gunawardena &
  Zittle; Richardson & Swan; Richardson et al. 2017 meta-analysis), with the measurement and
  re-examination caveats carried honestly (Tu; Terry & Doolittle); the CSCL corrective that providing
  a collaborative affordance is not the same as its activation — sociability must be designed for,
  not assumed (Kreijns, Kirschner & Jochems) — the field's own version of the F7 student-side
  activation gap; co-presence and collaboration in multi-user virtual worlds (De Back et al.;
  VanderMeer et al.). Prepares the literature base that M3.5/M4.2/M5.2 inherit rather than import
  mid-analysis. `[LIT-SLOT — populated from VR Pedagogy Secondary entry; selections provisional
  until full perusal]` `[PART I–II: co-disclosedness (Miterschlossenheit) (Part II §2);
  presence-as-floor extended to the social pole]`

## M2. The World and Its Deployment — Methods-Analogue
*Function: the VR article's Methods slot, recast: first the artifact as a virtual world and
rhetorical ecology (not a "platform" or "course shell"), then the cohort and instrument.*
`MAP:` absorbs §III.1.3–.4 and §III.3.1–.2 record material.

- **M2.1 The artifact.** The desktop clinical-immersion world described RODA-wise: the hospital
  hub and procedure rooms (the designed *Umwelt*); the filmed aisthēmata (OR footage, physician
  interviews, device animations); navigation and viewpoint (mouse-and-monitor embodiment); **the
  spatial proximity-voice co-watching capability and the procedure-paired group structure** — the
  ecology's authored WE. Every element named as designed archē. `[ANCHOR: F7 correction — platform
  facts, author-confirmed]` `[PART I–II: rhetorical ecology, wholly authored (Part II §3);
  producing-art/using-art]` `[NEW: the artifact has never been described in the dissertation's own vocabulary]`
- **M2.2 The cohort and the instrument.** Three terms (W25/S25/W26), N=241, 873 open responses;
  two strata (app ~51% / video-only ~44%, term-stable); coding record (codebook families,
  reliability .878, adjudication); standing limits stated once (single channel, retrospective,
  no learning-outcome claims). Band-R register. `[ANCHOR: 05-findings header; 00–03 survey-analysis]`
  `[REUSE-COMPRESS: survey-analysis 00–02]`
- **M2.3 The method of reading.** The chain as background grammar for survey data — which nodes are
  in play when students report presence, boredom, confusion; the two-channel rule as method (no
  bipolar construct); provenance registers as textual discipline. `[ANCHOR: cross-case §1;
  PART-III-OUTLINE §III.1.2]` `[PART I–II: A₀→A₄ (Part I §2); two-channel rule ← FCM apparatus]`

## M3. The Deployment Record — Results
*Function: the empirical core; findings presented in the order the student meets them: threshold →
world → flight → presence → the WE → the late question. Band R with Band-G hinges.*
`MAP:` = §III.3.3–.7 restructured; F-memo is the source of record.

- **M3.1 The threshold.** The geography of foreclosure: install/compatibility/hardware vs
  in-world friction; the world's first gate is the installer; the friction-prediction scorecard as
  falsifiable test (in-world stalls predicted, threshold stalls invisible from the dev machine).
  `[ANCHOR: F1, F2]` `[PART I–II: A₀ as horizon — availability as its deployment face]`
- **M3.2 A world to see, nothing to do.** D2's massive afford channel vs D3's absence; interactivity
  requests; monotony/passivity exemplars ("space of inactivity"; "not sure what exactly to be looking
  for" — the withheld *orekton*). `[ANCHOR: F3]` `[PART I–II: orekton; A₃→A₄]`
- **M3.3 The flight to video.** Two anatomies (excluded vs hassle-flight despite access); the
  effort-arithmetic verbatims; *Zeitvertreib* institutionalized as a course resource.
  `[ANCHOR: F4]` `[PART I–II: boredom's avoidance route; Part II's boring-world-as-orekton-fled]`
- **M3.4 Presence happens on screens.** F1-PRESENCE strata contrast; "feels like you are in it"
  as screen-route world-disclosedness attested verbatim; immersion-Yes ≈69% replicating the pilot's
  70% on the screen route; provisioning requests as students' own phantasia-load-gradient talk.
  `[ANCHOR: F7 first half]` `[PART I–II: world-disclosedness; data-discrepancy/phantasia-load]`
- **M3.5 The WE: had, wanted, unactivated.** ★ SPOTLIGHT MODULE. The corrected record in full:
  proximity-voice co-watching exists and every student is procedure-group-assigned; activators name
  co-watching the "main pro" (the WE *had*); non-activators report isolation (the WE *defaulted*,
  mis-attributed to design absence); "more directed collaboration" as a request to mandate the meet.
  The coordination cost: the differentiating affordance carries an activation energy the passive
  alternatives don't, so the convenience gradient cannibalizes precisely the affordance that answers
  "why not just YouTube?" `[ANCHOR: F7 correction, 2026-07-13 — the load-bearing empirical module]`
  `[PART I–II: co-disclosedness (Part II §2)]` `DEP: M3.3 (the gradient), M2.1 (platform facts)`
- **M3.6 From friction to justification.** The skepticism arc (frictions fall, value-skepticism
  rises 1.3→0.7→4.2); the divergence register sorted by the grid — form-1 majority with named
  culprits, the small no-culprit residue as second-form echo (single-channel ceiling stated).
  `[ANCHOR: F5, F6]` `[PART I–II: FCM second form; two-channel rule]`

## M4. Phenomenological Analysis — The Stalled Chain and the Answered Question
*Function: the payoff; the record read through the frame; Band G throughout. This is where H1,
the H3 clause, and the WE thesis are argued, in that order.*
`MAP:` = §III.4 material scoped to the deployment (lab keystone imported by reference only, per
the deferred arc decision).

- **M4.1 Completion, not bandwidth.** The stall's address: solicited at A₂/A₃ (the charged clinical
  aisthēmata), foreclosed at A₃→A₄ (no praxis, no needs-capture) — "a world that can only be watched
  has a boredom half-life." Boredom read as the diagnostic of mis-attunement between learner, task,
  and ecology: *Leergelassenheit* (withheld solicitation) meeting *Hingehaltenheit* (mandated duration
  without task). Boredom is never a stimulus property — the same footage is the most presence-praised
  AND most fled content. `[ANCHOR: cross-case §2(i)–(iii); F3]` `[PART I–II: the chain; the two
  moments ← FCM apparatus; energeia atelēs — engagement as incomplete actuality en route to completion]`
- **M4.2 The WE as the desktop's ontological differentiator.** ★ SPOTLIGHT MODULE. Incorporation is
  one in substance, dual in being — world-disclosedness AND co-disclosedness. The HMD route maximizes
  the world-pole and, in the published version, possessed no co-pole at all (solo entry; the article
  names it — and the co-pole was never subsequently built for VR, development having moved to the
  desktop route); the video route possesses neither in kind; the desktop route, thinner on
  phantasia-load, is *as deployed* the program's only route on which co-disclosedness is available —
  a de facto scope, stated as such, which sharpens rather than weakens the point: the WE is not a
  screen-native consolation but a developed asset this route alone carries. Watching-together in shared
  virtual space with proximate voice is not a feature but a mode of being-with: the WE the act
  presupposes and ratifies. The activation-energy finding then gets its full weight: the deployment's
  deepest loss is not presence but the WE left unconvened — a co-disclosedness the ecology holds open
  and the temporal economy lets lapse. `[NEW — the section's central theoretical contribution]`
  `[ANCHOR: F7 corrected; M3.5]` `[PART I–II: co-disclosedness; Burke consubstantiation → Miterschlossenheit;
  thymotic action's toward-whom (Part I §7) as the chain-side ground of the social]`
  `[LIT-SLOT: CSCL/co-presence/social-presence base prepared at M1.6 — inherit, cite-where-used]`
  `DEP: M1.6 (literature base)`
- **M4.3 Veri(dis)similitude's second face.** The H3 clause argued: for a screen-based world whose
  footage is one click away, the dissimilarity condition turns inward — different enough from the
  video of itself. The justification-demand is the cohort discovering this condition empirically;
  place, task, and the WE are the only materials the difference can be made of; the WE is the one
  of the three video cannot even approximate. `[NEW]` `[ANCHOR: F6; cross-case §2(v),(vii)]`
  `[PART I–II: veri(dis)similitude (Part II §3); route-not-kind differential]`
- **M4.4 What the desktop case gives back to the frame.** Route sets the load; the task sets the
  dwelling — the deployment shows the two poles' shared mechanism consummating (or stalling) at the
  same address Part II located analytically (A₃→A₄), now student-attested at N=241 scale. One
  paragraph, gesture-scale, on what only a headset deployment could test. `[ANCHOR: cross-case §2(vii),
  §3]` `[PART I–II: the media-differential claim — this sub-module partially performs Part II's
  promised closing differential at the empirical register; coordinate with Part II coda decision]`

## M5. Design — The Levers as Archai
*Function: from diagnosis to design; the five levers, with the WE-activation lever given its own
expanded movement.* `MAP:` = §III.5.2–.3 scoped to this section.

- **M5.1 The levers, ranked, as archai.** Each lever named as an archē — the productive source of an
  experiential pattern: threshold (re-admit the excluded) · task (open A₄; answers the
  justification-demand) · *orekton*-guidance (what to look for; captions) · WE-activation ·
  pacing/washout. `[ANCHOR: cross-case §3.3; deployment-brief §5]` `[PART I–II: archē, fourth sense
  (Part I §3 fn)]`
- **M5.2 Collapsing the activation energy of the WE.** ★ The expanded lever: the affordance and the
  grouping both exist; the design problem is temporal-economic — default/scheduled co-watch blocks,
  graded synchronous group sessions; offload the self-organization tax so the differentiator stops
  losing, every term, to the convenience gradient. NOT "build co-presence" (present), NOT "assign
  groups" (present). `[ANCHOR: F7 correction design brief]` `DEP: M4.2`
- **M5.3 The motto and the mirror.** Design against "why not just YouTube?" — every element must do
  something video cannot (task, place, together); the capture-economy as adversarial mirror (one
  breath); design as an ethical craft answerable for the dispositions it lays down.
  `[ANCHOR: cross-case §3.3]` `[PART I–II: Part II §4 "Carry-Over" ethics-of-design closing]`

